        "summary": "On desktop, the compact header bands on product screens (settings sections, product detail, cart, dashboard sub-pages) take their height from the art (about 375–440px), but they hold only a breadcrumb, an h2-size title and one line of lead text in the top-left corner. Half of each band is empty colour, and the form, cover, price or primary action starts at or below the middle of the first screen. In the reference, a tall band is earned by a full text block (headline, lead, checklist, pill; 02). Bands that only name the page stay short (04).",
        "samples": 1,
