          "pipeline/headspace-study/reference/set/02-desktop.png"
        ],
        "promptFix": "Size a compact header band by its text, not its art. Remove the art-derived min-height. The band is its text block plus `space.10` above and `space.8` below, about 200–260px on desktop and never more than a third of the first screen. The art box takes the trailing 40% of the band's width and is capped at the band's height. Its SVG uses a wide viewBox (about 400×200) with `height: 100%; width: auto; max-width: 100%`, so the scene spreads sideways instead of making the band taller. Only a front-page or landing hero, which carries a display headline, a lead and pills, may grow tall around its art. On a screen whose job is an action (a detail page with a buy action, a cart, a form), the item's cover or the first field must start within the first 600px of a desktop viewport.",
